  - toric variety
  - projective normality
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  A lattice polytope P has the integer decomposition property if, for every
  positive integer k, every lattice point of kP is a sum of k lattice points
  of P. Oda conjectured that every smooth lattice polytope has this property.
  We prove the conjecture for smooth lattice polytopes of dimension three with
  seven facets. Together with the known case of at most six facets, every
  smooth lattice 3-polytope with at most seven facets has the integer
  decomposition property. The proof combines three criteria on the normal fan,
  based on slicing and projection, with the classification of smooth
  projective toric threefolds of Picard number four; the finitely many
  certificates are checked in Lean 4.
